Three independent per-draw D3D12 loop optimizations, ported from the known-good Geometry Wars Retro
Evolved 2 Recompiled (5f4c05c) and Hard Corps Uprising Recompiled (8d03c63) commits. No behavioral
change in any of the three; only how the same result is computed.

Vertex buffer residency: InvalidateVertexBufferResidencyRange cleared vertex_buffers_in_sync_ one
fetch bit at a time. It now clears each 64-bit word it touches with one mask (built from the first and
last bit of the range within that word), handling a single-word range, a multi-word range, and bit 63
of a word the same way as the old per-bit loop did.

Float constant uploads: CopyUsedFloatConstants replaces one bit-scan-forward + one 16-byte memcpy per
used float constant with one memcpy per run of consecutive used constants (scanning the bitmap with
countr_zero/countr_one), applied to both the vertex and pixel float constant buffers. The resulting
constant buffer layout and ordering are unchanged.

Stencil bits: GetStencilBits/AddStencilBits looped tile-by-tile with `& (kEdramTileCount - 1)`
wraparound masking on every tile. They now normalize the start tile and clamp the length to the EDRAM
size up front, then process one contiguous run up to the end of the EDRAM and, only if the range
wraps, a second contiguous run from tile 0 - same OR semantics, no change to EDRAM ownership or
dirty-tile tracking.

